---
title: How to Configure Custom Quotation Number Format in Taskip
sidebar:
  order: 3
---
**Taskip allows you to personalize how quotation numbers are structured. This helps you stay organized, maintain consistency, and meet your business documentation standards.**

### **Steps to Configure Quotation Number Format**

*How to Set Up Automated Quotation Reminders in Taskip*

**1. Go to Settings\
Click Settings in the sidebar.**

**2. Select Quotation Settings\
Navigate to Quotation Settings.**

**3. Click the General Tab\
Open the General tab under Quotation Settings.**

### **Customization Options**

**Quotation Number Prefix\
Set a prefix to appear before the quotation number, such as `QT-`, `QUOTE-`, or `TASK-`.**

**Quotation Number Format\
Define your format using dynamic placeholders:**

{% table %}
- Placeholder
- Description
---
- `{year}`
- Current year (e.g., 2025)
---
- `{month}`
- Current month (e.g., 07)
---
- `{serial}`
- Simple incrementing number
---
- `{2_digit_serial}`
- Two-digit serial (01)
---
- `{3_digit_serial}`
- Three-digit serial (001)
---
- `{4_digit_serial}`
- Four-digit serial (0001)
---
- `{5_digit_serial}`
- Five-digit serial (00001)
---
- `{6_digit_serial}`
- Six-digit serial (000001)
{% /table %}

**Example Format:\
`QT-{year}-{month}-{4_digit_serial}`\
This will generate quotation numbers like `QT-2025-07-0001`.**

**Initial Number of the Quotation\
Set a starting value for the quotation serial. For instance, if you enter `301`, your first quotation number will be `QT-2025-07-0301`.**

**Save Changes\
Click Save Changes to activate the new format.**

### **Best Practices**

- **Use `{year}` and `{month}` to keep quotations chronological.**
- **Use a recognizable prefix for easy document filtering.**
- **Set an initial number if you’re continuing from another system.**

### **Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)**

### **Can I change the format later?**

**Yes, you can edit the format anytime. Previously issued quotations won’t be affected.**

### **Is the prefix mandatory?**

**No, but it’s helpful for clarity, especially if you issue different types of documents.**

### **Will quotation numbers reset yearly or monthly?**

**No. The numbering continues sequentially unless manually changed.**

### **Can I define a different format for each workspace or project?**

**Currently, the format is global within your Taskip workspace.**

### **Can I include a client’s name in the quotation number?**

**No, dynamic fields in quotation numbers are limited to date and serial elements.**
